Day 36/120 of my data analytics journey

A few days ago, I was stuck.

My KPI wouldn’t show.
My data model wasn’t making sense.

Fast forward to today…

I’ve completed the guided Power BI & SQL project, and here’s what the data revealed:

📌 Sales exceeded budget by $1M+
📌 Revenue is highly concentrated among top customers
📌 A few top products dominate sales, showing clear winners
📌 Sales steadily increased across the months, peaking toward year-end.

 Here are 3 key things I learned:
i) Data modeling is everything
If your relationships are wrong, your dashboard will confuse you

ii) SQL makes Power BI easier
Cleaning and structuring data upfront saves hours later

iii) Dashboards should tell a story, not just show numbers
Sales vs Budget, Customers, Products everything must connect.

This project pushed me, frustrated me, and taught me a lot.
But seeing the final dashboard…Totally worth it.

